CAT = "sgresRegulation"; SEG = "REG"
Q = [
("The Council for Estate Agencies was set up under the Estate Agents Act 2010 mainly to:",
 "Regulate agents and salespersons", ["Set prices for private property sales", "Build public housing", "Grant housing loans"],
 "CEA administers the Estate Agents Act to raise professionalism in the real estate agency industry and protect consumers. It does not set prices or lend money."),
("Under the Estate Agents Act, CEA licenses estate agents and:",
 "Registers salespersons", ["Licenses developers", "Approves bank loans", "Registers buyers"],
 "Estate agents (the agencies) are licensed and salespersons are registered with CEA. Housing developers are licensed under a different Act."),
("A salesperson acting for the seller of a private condo unit must not, for the same unit, also:",
 "Represent the buyer", ["Market it online", "Hold an open house", "Negotiate the price"],
 "The ban on dual representation means a salesperson cannot have both the seller and the buyer, or the landlord and the tenant, as clients for the same property."),
("A buyer hands the salesperson the option fee in cash to pass to the seller. The salesperson should:",
 "Decline to handle it", ["Hold it until completion", "Bank it in the agency's account", "Issue a receipt and keep it"],
 "Estate agents and salespersons must not hold or handle transaction monies such as option fees, deposits or rent. The parties pay each other or their lawyers directly."),
("A buyer is short of cash for the downpayment. Under CEA's rules, the salesperson must not:",
 "Refer him to a moneylender", ["Suggest he speak to banks about loans", "Explain the CPF rules", "Recommend legal advice"],
 "Salespersons are prohibited from referring clients to moneylenders, to protect consumers from taking on loans they cannot repay."),
("In an advertisement for a listing, a salesperson must not:",
 "Use CEA's logo", ["Show their registration number", "State their agency's name", "Give a contact number"],
 "Using the Council's name or logo in a way that suggests endorsement is not allowed. Name, registration number and agency details are required in property advertisements."),
("Besides their name as shown in the public register, a property advertisement by a salesperson must show:",
 "Their CEA registration number", ["Their sales record for this year", "The seller's NRIC number", "The owner's mortgage bank"],
 "Advertisements must carry the salesperson's name and registration number and the estate agent's name and licence number, so consumers can verify who they are dealing with."),
("Professional indemnity insurance held by estate agents mainly protects against:",
 "Claims for negligent work", ["Fire damage to listings", "Unpaid commissions", "A fall in property prices"],
 "PI insurance covers claims arising from errors, omissions or negligence in estate agency work, so that consumers can be compensated. It is a licensing requirement for estate agents."),
("A salesperson who has not met the yearly continuing professional development requirement risks:",
 "Non-renewal of registration", ["Paying a higher stamp duty on sales", "Losing CPF contributions", "A fine collected by HDB"],
 "Completing CPD is a condition for renewing registration, to keep salespersons' knowledge current with laws and practice."),
("Under CEA's Code of Ethics and Professional Client Care, a salesperson who receives a second offer for a listed property should:",
 "Convey it to the seller promptly", ["Hold it until the first lapses", "Tell the buyer to bid higher", "Pass it on only if it is the higher one"],
 "The Code requires salespersons to communicate all offers to clients in a timely manner, so the client decides. Filtering offers is not the salesperson's call."),
("A salesperson's brother wants to buy the seller's property. The salesperson should:",
 "Disclose it to the seller", ["Keep it confidential", "Lower the asking price", "Proceed without comment"],
 "Salespersons must make full disclosure of anything that could impair their independence, and minimise conflicts of interest. The client can then decide whether to proceed."),
("A seller asks whether he will owe income tax on his gain from the sale. The salesperson should:",
 "Suggest he ask a tax adviser", ["Tell him there is no tax", "Compute the tax himself", "Refuse to discuss the matter at all"],
 "The Code expects salespersons to recommend professional advice, from a lawyer, tax adviser or valuer, on matters beyond their own expertise."),
("A seller tells his salesperson the lowest price he will accept. The salesperson must:",
 "Keep it from buyers", ["Share it to close faster", "Put it in the listing", "Tell co-broking agents"],
 "Salespersons must safeguard confidential information about their client. Revealing the seller's bottom line would harm the seller's bargaining position."),
("Under the Code of Practice for Estate Agents, an estate agent must:",
 "Supervise its salespersons", ["Hold clients' deposits", "Set HDB resale prices", "Register its own salespersons"],
 "Estate agents are responsible for managing and supervising their salespersons, handling complaints and keeping records. CEA, not the agency, registers salespersons."),
("Which complaint can CEA act on?",
 "A salesperson's misleading ad", ["A buyer-seller defect dispute", "A rent dispute with no agent", "A bank's refusal of a loan"],
 "CEA handles complaints about the conduct of estate agents and salespersons. Contractual disputes between buyers and sellers, with no agent misconduct, are for the parties and the courts."),
("A consumer's dispute with an estate agent over commission is resolved under CEA's Dispute Resolution Scheme through:",
 "Mediation and arbitration", ["A trial before a CEA court judge", "A police investigation", "A hearing at HDB"],
 "CEA's Dispute Resolution Scheme offers mediation and, if needed, arbitration for disputes such as commission between consumers and estate agents."),
("A salesperson posts insulting comments about a rival agency's salespersons online. This breaches the duty to:",
 "Treat other agents fairly", ["Keep transaction records", "Avoid dual representation", "Disclose the commission"],
 "CEA's Practice Guidelines on conduct of estate agents and salespersons towards one another require them to act fairly and with respect, and not to bring the industry into disrepute."),
("Commission is generally earned by the agent who was the:",
 "Effective cause of the sale", ["First agent to list the property", "Last to show the unit", "Most senior in the agency"],
 "Under the law of agency, the agent who brings about the transaction, the effective cause, earns the commission, subject to the terms of the estate agency agreement."),
("To verify a private seller's ownership and any mortgage or caveat, a salesperson can buy a title search through:",
 "SLA's INLIS", ["URA's REALIS", "HDB's resale portal", "CEA's public register"],
 "The Integrated Land Information Service (INLIS) gives access to land title information, including ownership and encumbrances. REALIS holds market and transaction data."),
("Recent caveat-based transaction prices for private homes are best found in:",
 "URA's REALIS", ["SLA's INLIS", "CEA's public register", "HDB InfoWEB"],
 "URA's Real Estate Information System (REALIS) compiles private property transaction and supply data, which salespersons use to advise on pricing."),
("A buyer wants to check that a salesperson is properly registered. They should look up:",
 "CEA's public register", ["URA Space", "SLA's INLIS", "HDB InfoWEB"],
 "CEA's public register lists every registered salesperson and licensed estate agent, with any disciplinary record."),
("For property consumers, the Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act 2003 mainly covers claims about:",
 "Unfair practices by agents", ["Defects in a resale home", "Disputes over land title", "HDB refusals of eligibility to buy"],
 "The sale and purchase of property itself is largely excluded from the Act, but consumers can seek redress for unfair practices in estate agency services."),
("Which is an unfair practice under the Consumer Protection (Fair Trading) Act?",
 "Inventing rival offers", ["Quoting a fair market price", "Recommending a lawyer", "Showing a valuation report"],
 "Falsely claiming that other buyers have made offers, to pressure a consumer, is a deceptive and unfair practice. Consumers may seek redress, for example at the Small Claims Tribunals."),
("Carrying out estate agency work for a fee without being a registered salesperson is:",
 "An offence under the EAA", ["Allowed for one deal a year", "Allowed for relatives' homes", "Only a breach of contract"],
 "The Estate Agents Act makes it an offence to do estate agency work without a licence or registration. CEA can prosecute, and such persons may not be able to claim commission."),
]
